Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.  
The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).  
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.  

Task 1: Import assert.yml
Description Task 1: Import the assert.yml file

Task 2: Install required packages
Description Task 2: Install the required packages using the package module

Task 3: Configure systemd service
Description Task 3: Configure the systemd service using the template module, only when ansible_service_mgr is "systemd".

Task 4: Configure sysvinit service
Description Task 4: Configure the sysvinit service using the template module, only when ansible_service_mgr is "sysvinit", "upstart", or "openrc".

Task 5: Manage service
Description Task 5: Manage the service using the service module, with the name, state, and enabled parameters based on the item's definition in the service_list.

Task 6: Flush handlers
Description Task 6: Flush the handlers using the meta module.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook:
---
- name: Import assert.yml
  include_tasks: assert.yml

- name: Install required packages
  package:
    name:
      - python3
      - python3-pip
    state: present

- name: Configure systemd service
  template:
    src: service.j2
    dest: /etc/systemd/system/my_service.service
  when: ansible_service_mgr == "systemd"
  notify:
    - restart my_service

- name: Configure sysvinit service
  template:
    src: service.j2
    dest: /etc/init.d/my_service
  when: ansible_service_mgr in ["sysvinit", "upstart", "openrc"]
  notify:
    - restart my_service

- name: Manage service
  service:
    name: "{{ item.name }}"
    state: "{{ item.state }}"
    enabled: "{{ item.enabled }}"
  loop: "{{ service_list }}"

- name: Flush handlers
  meta: flush_handlers


