Task 1: Remove EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file if we're on Debian12
Description Task 1: This task removes the EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file if the python3 version installed is 3.11 on Debian12. This is related to a specific issue that can be found at https://github.com/geerlingguy/ansible-role-pip/issues/57

Task 2: debian12 | Get python3 version installed
Description Task 2: This task gets the python3 version installed on the system.

Task 3: debian12 | Remove EXTERNALLY-MANAGED
Description Task 3: This task removes the EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file from the system if the python3 version installed is 3.11 on Debian12.
..."


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---

- name: Remove EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file if we're on Debian12
  file:
    path: /etc/ansible/facts.d/externally_managed
    state: absent
  when: ansible_distribution == "Debian" and ansible_distribution_version == "12" and \
        python3_version == "3.11"

- name: debian12 | Get python3 version installed
  command: python3 --version 2>&1
  register: python3_version_output
  changed_when: false

- name: debian12 | Remove EXTERNALLY-MANAGED
  file:
    path: /etc/ansible/facts.d/externally_managed
    state: absent
  when: ansible_distribution == "Debian" and ansible_distribution_version == "12" and \
        python3_version_output.stdout == "Python 3.11.x"


